            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for is alive, then the Sanskrit for heats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: क्षमते",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क्षमते — kṣamate — \"forgives\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kṣamate is the present of the root √kṣam, \"to be patient, endure\", and so \"to pardon, forgive\" (MW). In the Rigveda it means \"is patient, endures\" (CDIAL 3657). Its noun kṣamā, \"patience, forgiveness\", went into Telugu and Kannada."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
